---
title: "getAllMembers (stem-bot-v2: src/api/members.ts)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_fetch_db: supabase.from(members).is(deleted_at, null)
    q_fetch_db --> q_err_db: error
    q_fetch_db --> q_check_empty: members loaded
    q_err_db --> [*]: res.status(500)
    q_check_empty --> q_respond_empty: !members or length === 0
    q_check_empty --> q_get_guild: members exist
    q_respond_empty --> [*]: res.json(data empty)

    q_get_guild --> q_err_guild: DISCORD_GUILD_ID not set
    q_get_guild --> q_iter_start: guild fetched
    q_err_guild --> [*]: res.status(500) Server configuration error

    q_iter_start --> q_map_members: Promise.all(members.map)
    q_map_members --> q_fetch_discord: guild.members.fetch(discord_uid)
    q_fetch_discord --> q_extract_name: discordMember found
    q_fetch_discord --> q_skip_null: member not found (returns null)
    q_extract_name --> q_parse_display: extract name from displayName before parenthesis
    q_parse_display --> q_map_result: return uid, name, username

    q_skip_null --> q_filter: null entry
    q_map_result --> q_filter: valid entry
    q_filter --> q_respond: filter out nulls
    q_respond --> [*]: res.json(success, data)

    note right of q_map_members
        INV-001: All Discord member fetches run in parallel via Promise.all (unbounded concurrency)
        INV-002: Discord API rate limits could cause partial failures
    end note

    note right of q_get_guild
        INV-003: Uses process.env.DISCORD_GUILD_ID directly instead of getGuildId() utility
    end note
